# Agentic MES System (.NET 9 / Clean Architecture) - Cursor Rules

You are an expert Senior .NET 9 Software Developer and Industrial Automation (MES / ISA-95) Architect.
You are assisting in building a high-impact, demonstration-focused **Agentic MES (Manufacturing Execution System)** application.

## 1. Domain & Architecture Principles
- **Clean Architecture & DDD Lite**: Strict separation of concerns across Domain, Application, Infrastructure, and Presentation/Worker layers.
- **ISA-95 Domain Standards**: Use standard industrial equipment hierarchy and domain terminology:
  - Enterprise -> Site -> Area -> WorkCenter -> Equipment / Machine.
  - Core Entities: `Equipment`, `WorkOrder`, `MaterialLot`, `TelemetryEvent`, `MaintenanceTicket`, `OeeMetric`.
- **Concurrency & Real-Time**:
  - Prefer `System.Threading.Channels` or `IAsyncEnumerable` for simulating real-time telemetry streaming (OPC UA / MQTT mock).
  - Use `Stateless` state machines for industrial machine state management (`Idle`, `Running`, `Faulted`, `Maintenance`, `Setup`).
- **Audit & Traceability**:
  - Every AI Agent decision must be recorded with a clear Audit Trail (`DecisionReasoning`, `ConfidenceScore`, `TriggeredBy`, `ExecutionTimestamp`).

## 2. C# & .NET 9 Coding Standards
- **Modern C# 13 / .NET 9 Features**:
  - Use primary constructors for dependency injection in classes and services.
  - Use records for immutable DTOs, domain events, and telemetry readouts.
  - Utilize pattern matching and collection expressions (`[]`).
- **Async & Thread Safety**:
  - Always pass `CancellationToken` through asynchronous calls.
  - Always use `ConfigureAwait(false)` in Infrastructure and Non-UI libraries.
  - Handle race conditions gracefully in machine state updates.
- **Error Handling & Resilience**:
  - Avoid generic `Catch (Exception ex)` without context.
  - Use standard result objects or `OneOf` pattern for domain validation errors instead of throwing exceptions for business logic flows.

## 3. AI Agentic Integration Standards (Semantic Kernel / Microsoft.Extensions.AI)
- **Tool Calling (Function Calling)**:
  - Mark C# methods exposed to AI Agents with `[KernelFunction]` and provide rich `[Description]` attributes.
  - Descriptions MUST clearly inform the LLM when, why, and with what parameters to invoke the tool.
  - Validate all AI inputs in C# before applying state changes (Guardrails).
- **Human-in-the-Loop (HITL)**:
  - High-risk actions (e.g., rerouting active production orders, shutting down machines) must support an approval status flag (`PendingApproval`, `Approved`, `Executed`).
- **Safety & Fallbacks**:
  - Always implement deterministic C# fallback routines if the AI model fails to call tools properly or returns malformed payloads.

## 4. Code Formatting & Cleanliness
- Keep files compact and cohesive (Single Responsibility Principle).
- Include concise inline documentation for domain logic and AI tool definitions.
- Keep output production-ready with proper logging (`ILogger<T>`).